 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.74,
   "text": "What if all the sun's output of visible light were bundled up into a laser-like beam that",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 3.74,
   "end": 6.04,
   "text": "had a diameter of around 1 meter once it reached the Earth?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 6.54,
   "end": 9.48,
   "text": "If you were standing in the path of the beam, you would obviously die pretty quickly.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 9.8,
   "end": 13.04,
   "text": "You wouldn't really die of anything in the traditional sense, you would just stop being",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 13.04,
   "end": 14.44,
   "text": "biology and start being physics.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 14.96,
   "end": 19.44,
   "text": "The Earth receives about .004% as much energy from the sun in an entire day as the sun",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 19.44,
   "end": 20.46,
   "text": "emits every second.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 20.88,
   "end": 23.7,
   "text": "When the beam of light hit the atmosphere, it would heat the air to millions of degrees",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 23.7,
   "end": 26.7,
   "text": "in a fraction of a second, turning into a plasma which would start dumping its heat",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 26.7,
   "end": 27.62,
   "text": "as a flood of x-rays.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.128,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 27.62,
   "end": 31.44,
   "text": "Those x-rays would heat up the air around them which would turn to plasma itself, albeit",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 31.44,
   "end": 33.54,
   "text": "a cooler plasma, and start emitting infrared light.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 33.92,
   "end": 36.92,
   "text": "The radiation would vaporize everything in sight and start stripping away the Earth's",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 36.92,
   "end": 39.26,
   "text": "surface, like a hydrogen bomb, only much more violent.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 39.72,
   "end": 43.14,
   "text": "But the Earth is big enough to protect people on the other side, at least for a bit, from",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 43.14,
   "end": 44.38,
   "text": "the direct effects of the sun beam.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 44.66,
   "end": 47.6,
   "text": "They're still not going to make it, but what exactly would they die from?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 48.44,
   "end": 49.52,
   "text": "Turns out, twilight.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 50.04,
   "end": 51.38,
   "text": "Or moonlight, it depends on the details.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 52.08,
   "end": 55.38,
   "text": "Twilight is light from the out-of-sight sun that reaches you by scattering off the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 55.38,
   "end": 55.78,
   "text": "atmosphere.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.153,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.012
  },
  {
   "start": 55.78,
   "end": 59.3,
   "text": "When the beam of light hit the Earth, everything from infrared radiation to x-rays",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 59.3,
   "end": 61.32,
   "text": "would flood into the atmosphere, turning it to plasma.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 61.76,
   "end": 65.22,
   "text": "Plasma is relatively transparent to x-rays, so those would pass through and dump their",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 65.22,
   "end": 68.46,
   "text": "energy into the non-plasma air around it, heating it enough to give off its own",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 68.46,
   "end": 69.6,
   "text": "substantial thermal radiation.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 70.02,
   "end": 72.88,
   "text": "In general, a lot of this radiation would escape into space, where we don't",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 72.88,
   "end": 74.98,
   "text": "need to worry about it unless the Earth reflected back to Earth.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 75.4,
   "end": 78.08,
   "text": "Unfortunately, a portion of the radiation would stay within the atmosphere.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 78.48,
   "end": 81.22,
   "text": "A bubble of heat and light would wrap around the Earth, a twilight inferno",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 81.22,
   "end": 83.22,
   "text": "rapidly heating the atmosphere and surface as it went.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.097,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 83.22,
   "end": 86.54,
   "text": "What's more, much of the matter around the sun beam's contact point would be",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 86.54,
   "end": 89.88,
   "text": "blasted into space, where it would reflect infrared light back down beyond",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 89.88,
   "end": 90.36,
   "text": "the horizon.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 90.84,
   "end": 93.06,
   "text": "When the device kicked in, the moon would go dark, since the sunlight",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 93.06,
   "end": 95.3,
   "text": "illuminating it would be funneled into the beam that's destroying the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 95.3,
   "end": 95.64,
   "text": "atmosphere.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 96.04,
   "end": 98.9,
   "text": "The intense light from the destruction would itself, however, illuminate the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 98.9,
   "end": 102.2,
   "text": "moon, and this reflected moonlight alone could be enough to burn you to",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 102.2,
   "end": 104.88,
   "text": "death, just in time for the incendiary twilight to wrap around the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 104.88,
   "end": 106.58,
   "text": "planet, bringing on one final sunrise.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 107.18,
   "end": 108.9,
   "text": "But Earth might not be entirely doomed.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 109.24,
   "end": 111.94,
   "text": "The Earth can only spend a maximum of about seven minutes in the path of",
   "avg_logprob": -0.079,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.015
  },
  {
   "start": 112.08,
   "end": 113.96,
   "text": "the beam before our orbit carries us out of the way.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.076
  },
  {
   "start": 114.4,
   "end": 116.92,
   "text": "Everyone on the surface would still be cooked, of course, and much of the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.076
  },
  {
   "start": 116.92,
   "end": 119.4,
   "text": "atmosphere and exterior would be lost, but the bulk of the Earth would",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.076
  },
  {
   "start": 119.4,
   "end": 122.52,
   "text": "probably remain, as a testament to humanity's horrible ideas.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.076
  }
 ],
